--- BUF-06: append past a fixed buffer's capacity truncates at capacity ---
a buffer called cupboard is 25 bytes.
a boolean called 'cupboard found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'cupboard found an error already pending' to true.
a boolean called 'cupboard overflowed' is false.
append "y6p8h43e9dzjrnrst5mbcxielsxvvorkec7tegz47yqesry1br8l1yb2fwk4k9h8hevfcd15ip3er8c8aav1neoqx8uysfot5a4vr75as7kp7z9fruwzef4g8znl8gs2h58y" to cupboard.
On error Set 'cupboard overflowed' to true.
If 'cupboard overflowed' is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-06: expected 1 got {'cupboard overflowed'}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard overflowed'.
If cupboard's size is not 25 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-06: expected 25 got {cupboard's size}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's size.
a text called 'cupboard captured content' is cupboard as text.
If cupboard is not "y6p8h43e9dzjrnrst5mbcxiel" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-06: expected y6p8h43e9dzjrnrst5mbcxiel got {'cupboard captured content'}", Exit 95. Print cupboard.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called cupboard is 25 bytes,
  a boolean called 'cupboard found an error already pending' is false,
  On error Set 'cupboard found an error already pending' to true,
  a boolean called 'cupboard overflowed' is false,
  append "y6p8h43e9dzjrnrst5mbcxielsxvvorkec7tegz47yqesry1br8l1yb2fwk4k9h8hevfcd15ip3er8c8aav1neoqx8uysfot5a4vr75as7kp7z9fruwzef4g8znl8gs2h58y" to cupboard,
  On error Set 'cupboard overflowed' to true,
  If 'cupboard overflowed' is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-06: expected 1 got {'cupboard overflowed'}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard overflowed',
  If cupboard's size is not 25 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-06: expected 25 got {cupboard's size}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's size,
  a text called 'cupboard captured content' is cupboard as text,
  If cupboard is not "y6p8h43e9dzjrnrst5mbcxiel" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-06: expected y6p8h43e9dzjrnrst5mbcxiel got {'cupboard captured content'}", Exit 95. Print cupboard.

--- BUF-15, BUF-16, BUF-17: resize, grow-preserves, shrink-truncates ---
a buffer called 'the inbox' is 51 bytes in size.
append "stwumzsydfbajh2001jwpil3heuyo" to 'the inbox'.
reallocate 'the inbox' to 89 bytes.
If 'the inbox's capacity is not 89 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-15: expected 89 got {'the inbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's capacity.
a text called 'the inbox grown content' is 'the inbox' as text.
If 'the inbox' is not "stwumzsydfbajh2001jwpil3heuyo" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-16: expected stwumzsydfbajh2001jwpil3heuyo got {'the inbox grown content'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox'.
resize 'the inbox' to 13 bytes.
If 'the inbox's capacity is not 13 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-15: expected 13 got {'the inbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's capacity.
If 'the inbox's size is not 13 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-17: expected 13 got {'the inbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's size.
a text called 'the inbox shrunk content' is 'the inbox' as text.
If 'the inbox' is not "stwumzsydfbaj" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-17: expected stwumzsydfbaj got {'the inbox shrunk content'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'the inbox' is 51 bytes in size,
  append "stwumzsydfbajh2001jwpil3heuyo" to 'the inbox',
  reallocate 'the inbox' to 89 bytes,
  If 'the inbox's capacity is not 89 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-15: expected 89 got {'the inbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's capacity,
  a text called 'the inbox grown content' is 'the inbox' as text,
  If 'the inbox' is not "stwumzsydfbajh2001jwpil3heuyo" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-16: expected stwumzsydfbajh2001jwpil3heuyo got {'the inbox grown content'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox',
  resize 'the inbox' to 13 bytes,
  If 'the inbox's capacity is not 13 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-15: expected 13 got {'the inbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's capacity,
  If 'the inbox's size is not 13 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-17: expected 13 got {'the inbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's size,
  a text called 'the inbox shrunk content' is 'the inbox' as text,
  If 'the inbox' is not "stwumzsydfbaj" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-17: expected stwumzsydfbaj got {'the inbox shrunk content'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox'.

--- BUF-29, BUF-30: write bound is capacity, read bound is size ---
a buffer called 'the dispatch note' is 24 bytes.
append "hquiih" to 'the dispatch note'.
a boolean called 'the dispatch note found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'the dispatch note found an error already pending' to true.
a boolean called 'the dispatch note write errored' is false.
Set byte 17 of 'the dispatch note' to 32.
On error Set 'the dispatch note write errored' to true.
If 'the dispatch note write errored' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-29: expected 0 got {'the dispatch note write errored'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note write errored'.
If 'the dispatch note's size is not 17 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-29: expected 17 got {'the dispatch note's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's size.
a boolean called 'the dispatch note gap read errored' is false.
a number called 'the dispatch note gap read' is byte 20 of 'the dispatch note'.
On error Set 'the dispatch note gap read errored' to true.
If 'the dispatch note gap read errored' is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-30: expected 1 got {'the dispatch note gap read errored'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note gap read errored'.
If 'the dispatch note gap read' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-30: expected 0 got {'the dispatch note gap read'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note gap read'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'the dispatch note' is 24 bytes,
  append "hquiih" to 'the dispatch note',
  a boolean called 'the dispatch note found an error already pending' is false,
  On error Set 'the dispatch note found an error already pending' to true,
  a boolean called 'the dispatch note write errored' is false,
  Set byte 17 of 'the dispatch note' to 32,
  On error Set 'the dispatch note write errored' to true,
  If 'the dispatch note write errored' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-29: expected 0 got {'the dispatch note write errored'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note write errored',
  If 'the dispatch note's size is not 17 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-29: expected 17 got {'the dispatch note's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's size,
  a boolean called 'the dispatch note gap read errored' is false,
  a number called 'the dispatch note gap read' is byte 20 of 'the dispatch note',
  On error Set 'the dispatch note gap read errored' to true,
  If 'the dispatch note gap read errored' is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-30: expected 1 got {'the dispatch note gap read errored'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note gap read errored',
  If 'the dispatch note gap read' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-30: expected 0 got {'the dispatch note gap read'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note gap read'.

--- BUF-33: clear sets size to 0 and preserves capacity - fixed form ---
a buffer called 'scratch' is 14 bytes.
append "c3" to 'scratch'.
a number called 'scratch capacity before clearing' is 'scratch's capacity.
clear 'scratch'.
If 'scratch's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-33: expected 0 got {'scratch's size}", Exit 95. Print 'scratch's size.
If 'scratch's capacity is not 'scratch capacity before clearing' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-33: expected {'scratch capacity before clearing'} got {'scratch's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'scratch's capacity.

--- BUF-33 again - dynamic form draws too ---
Create a buffer called 'the register' with size 9.
append "zkdzrdc" to 'the register'.
a number called 'the register capacity before clearing' is 'the register's capacity.
clear 'the register'.
If 'the register's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-33: expected 0 got {'the register's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's size.
If 'the register's capacity is not 'the register capacity before clearing' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-33: expected {'the register capacity before clearing'} got {'the register's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's capacity.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'scratch' is 14 bytes,
  append "c3" to 'scratch',
  a number called 'scratch capacity before clearing' is 'scratch's capacity,
  clear 'scratch',
  If 'scratch's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-33: expected 0 got {'scratch's size}", Exit 95. Print 'scratch's size,
  If 'scratch's capacity is not 'scratch capacity before clearing' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-33: expected {'scratch capacity before clearing'} got {'scratch's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'scratch's capacity.

--- BUF-11: length is size, mutation drawn - append branch ---
Create a buffer called 'the register' with size 26.
append "bsjqzlxnpnciv1zqmrbpt9" to 'the register'.
If 'the register's length is not 'the register's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'the register's size} got {'the register's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's length.
append "8" to 'the register'.
If 'the register's length is not 'the register's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'the register's size} got {'the register's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's length.

--- BUF-11 again - set-byte branch ---
a buffer called pantry is 26 bytes in size.
append "z3zy8bcrws00fpl8" to pantry.
If pantry's length is not pantry's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {pantry's size} got {pantry's length}", Exit 95. Print pantry's length.
Set byte 3 of pantry to 231.
If pantry's length is not pantry's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {pantry's size} got {pantry's length}", Exit 95. Print pantry's length.

--- BUF-11 again - clear branch ---
a buffer called 'scratch' is 25 bytes in size.
append "g4c" to 'scratch'.
If 'scratch's length is not 'scratch's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'scratch's size} got {'scratch's length}", Exit 95. Print 'scratch's length.
clear 'scratch'.
If 'scratch's length is not 'scratch's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'scratch's size} got {'scratch's length}", Exit 95. Print 'scratch's length.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  Create a buffer called 'the register' with size 26,
  append "bsjqzlxnpnciv1zqmrbpt9" to 'the register',
  If 'the register's length is not 'the register's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'the register's size} got {'the register's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's length,
  append "8" to 'the register',
  If 'the register's length is not 'the register's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'the register's size} got {'the register's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's length.

